@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il27-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il27-tax-years`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance s 39A — "זיכוי לחייל משוחרר", the credit for a discharged soldier. Row IL-27.
-- Source lines 1609-1617.
--
-- A fraction of a credit point for each month of the first 36 months after the month in which he ended his regular service:
-- one sixth if he served 23 full months (a man) or 22 (a woman) or more; one twelfth if he served less. The credit is brought into
-- "the calculation of the tax on his income from personal exertion": the points are the section's answer, and the tax they are set
-- against is the composer's (as for s 40(b)(1A), fork F17 of row IL-08).
--
-- MONTHS. The months are calendar months, the month of discharge not counted (it is the month "after" which the 36 begin), and a
-- tax year is the calendar year, so the points for a tax year are the number of its months that fall within the 36, times the
-- fraction. The Discharged Soldiers Absorption Law of 5754-1994, which defines "discharged soldier" and "regular service", is not
-- in the source bundle; whether one is a discharged soldier, and his full months of service, are facts the caller states.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 39A — credit for a discharged soldier`

-- src:1610 | בחישוב המס על הכנסתו מיגיעה אישית של חייל משוחרר תובא בחשבון חלק מנקודת זיכוי לכל חודש משלושים וששה החודשים הראשונים שלאחר החודש שבו סיים את שירותו הסדיר, כמפורט להלן:
-- src:1611 | (1) 1 ⁄ 6 נקודת זיכוי – אם שירת שירות סדיר של –
-- src:1612 | (א) לגבי גבר – 23 חודשים מלאים לפחות;
-- src:1613 | (ב) לגבי אישה – 22 חודשים מלאים לפחות;
-- src:1614 | (2) 1 ⁄ 12 נקודת זיכוי – אם שירת שירות סדיר של פחות מ –
-- src:1615 | (א) לגבי גבר – 23 חודשים מלאים;
-- src:1616 | (ב) לגבי אישה – 22 חודשים מלאים;
-- src:1617 | לענין זה, ”חייל משוחרר“ ו”שירות סדיר“ – כהגדרתם בחוק קליטת חיילים משוחררים, התשנ״ד–1994.

-- (1)(a), (b), (2)(a), (b): the full months of regular service that give one sixth of a point, by sex.
@ref ITO s 39A(1)(a), (b), (2)(a), (b), lines 1612-1613, 1615-1616
GIVEN i IS A `A discharged soldier in a tax year, for section 39A`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 39A — the full months of regular service that give one sixth of a point to` i MEANS
    CONSIDER i's `sex`
    WHEN `a man`   THEN 23
    WHEN `a woman` THEN 22

@ref ITO s 39A(1), (2), lines 1611, 1614
GIVEN i IS A `A discharged soldier in a tax year, for section 39A`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 39A — the fraction of a point for each month, for` i MEANS
    IF   i's `full months of regular service` AT LEAST `s 39A — the full months of regular service that give one sixth of a point to` i
    THEN 1/6
    ELSE 1/12

-- The months of the tax year within "the first 36 months after the month in which he ended his regular service".
@ref ITO s 39A, line 1610
GIVEN i IS A `A discharged soldier in a tax year, for section 39A`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 39A — the months of the tax year within the 36 months after discharge, for` i MEANS
    max 0 (min (`the last month of the tax year`) (`the last month of the 36`) MINUS max (`the first month of the tax year`) (`the first month of the 36`) PLUS 1)
    WHERE
        `the month of discharge`   MEANS `the month count of calendar month` (i's `calendar month in which he ended his regular service`) `of` (i's `calendar year in which he ended his regular service`)
        `the first month of the 36` MEANS `the month of discharge` PLUS 1
        `the last month of the 36`  MEANS `the month of discharge` PLUS 36
        `the first month of the tax year` MEANS `the month count of calendar month` 1 `of` (i's `tax year`)
        `the last month of the tax year`  MEANS `the month count of calendar month` 12 `of` (i's `tax year`)

@ref ITO s 39A, lines 1610-1617; fork F1 (residence)
GIVEN r IS A `A reading of the sections that name no residence condition (ss 39A, 39B, 40A, 40B)`
      i IS A `A discharged soldier in a tax year, for section 39A`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 39A, reading the residence condition as` r `, for` i MEANS
    `for tax year` (i's `tax year`) `, row IL-27 answers`
        (`the points, unless section 48A may take them from a foreign worker:` (i's `a foreign worker`) `,`
            (`points under a section that names no residence condition, for` (i's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`) `, the points being` `the points` `, reading the condition as` r))
    WHERE
        `the points` MEANS
            IF   i's `a discharged soldier within the Discharged Soldiers Absorption Law`
            THEN `s 39A — the months of the tax year within the 36 months after discharge, for` i TIMES `s 39A — the fraction of a point for each month, for` i
            ELSE 0

-- At the reading the switch names: declined where residence decides.
@export The credit points under Income Tax Ordinance s 39A (discharged soldier) for a tax year from 2024: a sixth or a twelfth of a point for each month of the first 36 months after the month in which regular service ended, set against the tax on income from personal exertion; declines for one who is not an Israeli resident, and for a foreign worker (s 48A)
@ref ITO s 39A, lines 1610-1617
GIVEN i IS A `A discharged soldier in a tax year, for section 39A`
          @desc the tax year, residence, sex, whether he is a discharged soldier, his full months of regular service, and the calendar month and year in which he ended it
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 39A for` i MEANS
    `the credit points under section 39A, reading the residence condition as` `the reading row IL-27 takes of the sections that name no residence condition` `, for` i

-- The credit in NIS: the points times the value of a credit point (s 33A), which is an input (rows IL-01 and IL-03).
@ref ITO s 39A, s 33A
GIVEN i IS A `A discharged soldier in a tax year, for section 39A`
      `the value of one credit point` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit under section 39A, in NIS, for` i `, at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point` MEANS
    `the credit points under section 39A for` i TIMES `the value of one credit point`
